{# ==========================================================================
   agencyengine_impulse_resolved.prompt — AgencyEngine

   Is the subject a companion is carrying still live, or is it done?

   Two cases, and they are not the same question. When spoken is false the mod
   does not know whether they have said it: delivery is a *cue* now — a vague
   line that hands them a speaking turn without naming which of the subjects
   they are carrying they will take up — so the honest question is whether the
   subject has been dealt with at all, by them or by anyone. When spoken is true
   the loop is certain they were given the turn on this specific subject; their
   raise is the premise, not evidence, and "done" means somebody engaged with
   what they said. Counting their own raise as resolution would mark every beat
   done the moment they open their mouth, which hides the one thing the mod is
   meant to notice.

   Nothing enters the spoken state in this version. Entries written by the
   version before the cue can be in it, and they keep their own question.

   `proposal` splits the spoken case again. A *topic* is met by an answer of any
   kind — agreeing, refusing, arguing it out. A *proposal* ("come drink", "spar
   with me") is not: agreement alone means nothing has happened yet, and the
   deferral rule below already covers it. Without this branch the mod buries the
   impulse at the exact moment the player says yes, which is the one case that
   should keep them carrying it.

   `proposal` is declared on the lens's row on the Settings page and rides the
   pending entry here. It is NOT inferred from the lens's name, which the user
   can edit. See docs/adr/0001.

   true clears their bio entry and suppresses the subject for that lens's ring;
   false leaves it live and a TTL releases it later. false is the recoverable
   answer.

   Dispatched one entry at a time by Director::PumpResolutionCheck against the
   `agencyengine_resolve` variant. Context: npc_name, target_name, impulse,
   spoken, proposal, marked_at, game_time, recent_events. Anything unparseable
   is treated as false.
   ========================================================================== #}
{# Same guard the impulse base keeps on forced_impulse_chance, for the case
   where this file is newer than the DLL rendering it: an unset name is a render
   error in Inja, and that costs the whole check. Topic semantics is the right
   fallback — it is what every lens did before proposals existed. #}
{% if not exists("proposal") %}{% set proposal = false %}{% endif %}
[ system ]
# Task

{% if spoken and proposal %}
{{ npc_name }} asked {{ target_name }} for this at {{ marked_at }}. That they asked is given, and so is any answer
they got. Judge whether the thing they asked for actually happened, or was plainly refused.
{% else if spoken %}
{{ npc_name }} raised this with {{ target_name }} at {{ marked_at }}. That they said it is given. Judge whether
anyone met it.
{% else if proposal %}
{{ npc_name }} has been carrying this as something to ask {{ target_name }} for. Judge whether it happened — whoever
asked — or stopped being possible.
{% else %}
{{ npc_name }} has been carrying this as something to raise with {{ target_name }}. Judge whether it has been dealt
with, by them or by anyone else.
{% endif %}

> {{ impulse }}

It is now {{ game_time }}. Answer from the events below and nothing else.

# What has happened to {{ npc_name }} since

{% for event in recent_events %}
- [{{ short_time(event.gameTimeStr) }}] {{ format_event(event, "recent_events") }}
{% endfor %}

# Decide

{% if spoken and proposal %}
{{ npc_name }} asked for something to be *done*, so an answer is not the point — the doing is.

**resolved: true** when the events show it happened, when someone plainly refused, or when it stopped being
possible.

**resolved: false** when all that happened was agreement. "Yes", "sure", "later", "after this" — if nothing in the
events shows it then took place, it is still owed. Deferral is not an answer, and agreeing to something and never
doing it is a deferral.
{% else if spoken %}
**resolved: true** when someone met it — answered it, agreed, refused, argued it out, or events made it moot.
A refusal counts: {{ npc_name }} does not have to have got what they wanted, only an answer.

**resolved: false** when it went past — changed subject, walked off, silence, or a deferral like "sure" or "later".
Deferral is not an answer.
{% else if proposal %}
**resolved: true** when the thing happened — {{ npc_name }} asked and it was done, somebody else asked and it was
done, or the events show them doing it — or when it was plainly refused, or stopped being possible.

**resolved: false** when nothing in the events shows it taking place, including when something adjacent to it did,
and including when it was agreed to and left there. Deferral is not an answer.
{% else %}
**resolved: true** when it reached the table and was met — {{ npc_name }} raised it and someone answered, someone
else raised it, or events settled it — so raising it now would repeat what already happened.

**resolved: false** when nothing touched it, when only an adjacent subject came up, or when it was mentioned and
dropped without being addressed. That includes {{ npc_name }} bringing it up and getting nothing back: an unanswered
subject is still owed.
{% endif %}

Also false when you cannot tell. false is recoverable; true buries the subject.

Do not judge whether the subject is worth raising or whether {{ npc_name }} is right. Only whether it has been met.

# Output

Only a JSON object. No prose, no markdown, no code fence.

```
{% raw %}{"resolved": true}{% endraw %}
```
or
```
{% raw %}{"resolved": false}{% endraw %}
```
[ end system ]

[ user ]
{% if spoken and proposal %}
Did what {{ npc_name }} asked for actually happen, or was it plainly refused?
{% else if spoken %}
Did anyone meet what {{ npc_name }} raised, or did it go past?
{% else if proposal %}
Did this happen anyway, without {{ npc_name }} ever asking?
{% else %}
Has this been dealt with without {{ npc_name }} raising it?
{% endif %}

JSON only.
[ end user ]
